{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Partial_Proof)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Partial Proof)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Lazy_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Lazy solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Even_Lazier_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Even Lazier Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Algebraic_Insight_into_Given_Property\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Algebraic Insight into Given Property</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35fba6f1786c98e4eb4d4db3d7fe553d2306dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_{2018}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"117\" height=\"11\" /> be a strictly increasing sequence of positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e35b1c41550901c31e792bc521651ff1b285b18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{2018}=2018^{2018}.\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />\nWhat is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680816d1a06d6730157a7350902257357c166bad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^3+a_2^3+\\cdots+a_{2018}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/d/3ad07ba45d9a4dcd46fbd971320abb2585f7ce0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Verify that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840bfe60acda2b8077efce0f4ae2adc6a98fde4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 \\equiv a \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"21\" /> manually for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a51d79ef0404dabc277126bcb1171b2127e83cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in \\mathbb{Z}/6\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />. We check: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/f/d8f8e1fc160363584a7db75dd7a0efb8630c02cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a428f73df568f0f1107160af3d6226bb57d3a6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^3 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60224689062bdb777e8419ba4212ad9e942f3a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 \\equiv 8 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/014728f7c131805079e36844804c17a89bea28e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^3 \\equiv 27 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"21\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fc7bc241c6a5ea6ed925dc25829d884e3909375.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^3 \\equiv 64 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33887fb0c7ade7c5a3bf01d7cc949732477e085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3 \\equiv 125 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" />. We conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840bfe60acda2b8077efce0f4ae2adc6a98fde4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 \\equiv a \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f7893407393a755d837fda2f8f08e6da74d772a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1^3+a_2^3+\\cdots+a_{2018}^3 \\equiv a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{2018}\\pmod{6}.\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/67324af8319b743b95edfe3edf9b33bd24395c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2018^{2018} = 1009^{2018} \\cdot 2^{2018} \\equiv \\boxed{ \\text{(E)}4} \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"344\" height=\"30\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/0/da0e8eaf92090fade8099e83d28191ca138d750a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> alternates with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> increases, and by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler%27s_Totient_Theorem\" title=\"Euler&#39;s Totient Theorem\">Euler's Totient Theorem</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0ce9f5b837b3fea4a57af3070a7356f036869e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1009^{2018} = (1009^2)^{1009} \\equiv 1^{1009} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"341\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>~Dolphindesigner\n</p><p>~Major error correction made by akashsuresh1.22~\n</p><p>~Another major error correction made by YTH\n</p><p>~Glossed-over detail filled in by GAMER100\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c71d7df6e6b31de3d6cd9f3cb6aa4a315d6178cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{2018}\\right)^3=a_1^3+a_2^3+\\cdots+a_{2018}^3+3a_1^2\\left(a_1+a_2\\\\ +\\cdots+a_{2018}-a_1\\right)+3a_2^2\\left(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{2018}-a_2\\right)+\\cdots+3a_{2018}^2\\left(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{2018}-a_{2018}\\right)+6\\sum_{i\\neq j\\neq k}^{2018} a_ia_ja_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -26px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"82\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197340650e3c2c9bc6755fdc2373be762ccef242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^3+a_2^3+\\cdots+a_{2018}^3+3a_1^2\\left(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{2018}-a_1\\right)+3a_2^2\\left(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{2018}-a_2\\right)+\\cdots+3a_{2018}^2\\left(a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_{2018}-a_{2018}\\right)+6\\sum_{i\\neq j\\neq k}^{2018} a_ia_ja_k\\equiv a_1^3+a_2^3+\\cdots+a_{2018}^3+3a_1^2({2018}^{2018}-a_1)+3a_2^2({2018}^{2018}-a_2)+\\cdots+3a_{2018}^2({2018}^{2018}-a_{2018}) \\equiv -2(a_1^3+a_2^3+\\cdots+a_{2018}^3)\\pmod 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"1049\" height=\"97\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a4699aa0a2c27c1825b922fbf1bb09cffb82158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2(a_1^3+a_2^3+\\cdots+a_{2018}^3)\\equiv \\left(2018^{2018}\\right)^3\\equiv\\left( 2^{2018}\\right)^3\\equiv 4^3\\equiv 4\\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"537\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/79868c7c333745def943e99e5418e69888dd1ab1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^3+a_2^3+\\cdots+a_{2018}^3\\equiv 1\\pmod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"19\" />. However, since cubing preserves parity, and the sum of the individual terms is even, the sum of the cubes is also even, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b4198920681ecb231a4fd1c42717a4272ee37de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"50\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Partial_Proof.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Partial_Proof)\">Solution 3 (Partial Proof)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Partial Proof)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can not \nassume that the problem will have a consistent answer for all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. For the purpose of this solution, we will assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b1171ce641826e9aca894162f9c15a57f6b46e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We first note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e416b9bc91aef03c7fefbcc4485a3bad8147582a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^3+2^3+...+n^3 = (1+2+...+n)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"19\" />. So what we are trying to find is what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81dff7eb627ecfbab7aa55fc30d726d7729bbd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(2018^{2018}\\right)^2=\\left(2018^{4036}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"189\" height=\"25\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We start by noting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a46b5b3929665fcb2500f3583ab77297a85afd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2018$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/9/8995349b4c40c35f43a787ec45878c8b3b8a3f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. So we are trying to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/4/ae498773839f561a51a6e68a3087ddfdc18e0a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(2^{4036}\\right) \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"130\" height=\"23\" />. Instead of trying to do this with some number theory skills, we could just look for a pattern. We start with small powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e68ad31d12ba3d14b80a9341ee44e6238555124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a4ab443c94f13ae3ad0efbc8c6fa07b58a930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420813c47b9ba0edd71bba84716bd485967ac81a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and so on... So we see that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/194c7412b70f0d798edcd5d294cede056e328ea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(2^{4036}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"50\" height=\"22\" /> has an even power, it must be congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b80757868a4e2333d6ff695bd7e9cb3abf5cc0cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, thus giving our answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b4198920681ecb231a4fd1c42717a4272ee37de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(E) }4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"50\" height=\"28\" />. You can prove this pattern using mods. But I thought this was easier.\n</p><p>-TheMagician\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Lazy_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Lazy_solution)\">Solution 4 (Lazy solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Lazy solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can assume that the problem will have a consistent answer for all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. For the purpose of this solution, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea13ffd7a10964f916c7cdc6849852a2c796ddd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, ... a_{2017}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"11\" /> are multiples of 6 and find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31ae1dfcf58dab9ca99370c804ac23e235c131bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2018^{2018} \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" /> (which happens to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/225544c15b567b5890d0b84da94ba99e1e167751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${a_1}^3 + ... + {a_{2018}}^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d802474bd3da5744538ae57af1b55124cbd6b569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> or just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982a88b67a2e4cfdf06eb9e75b1d5ecfcd482884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}  4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"48\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>-Patrick4President\n</p><p>~minor edit made by CatachuKetchup~\n</p><p>WARNING: Technique does not always work; you have been warned\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Even_Lazier_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Even_Lazier_Solution)\">Solution 5 (Even Lazier Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Even Lazier Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Due to the large amounts of variables in the problem, and the fact that the test is only 75 minutes, you can assume that the answer is probably just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31ae1dfcf58dab9ca99370c804ac23e235c131bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2018^{2018} \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982a88b67a2e4cfdf06eb9e75b1d5ecfcd482884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}  4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"48\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ Zeeshan12 [Be warned that this technique is not recommended for all problems and you should use it as a last resort]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Algebraic_Insight_into_Given_Property\">Algebraic Insight into Given Property</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Algebraic Insight into Given Property\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Mods is a good way to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f08da8228aea42b6adac3e93948bc700c3c151b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 \\equiv a \\pmod6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />: residues are simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718e9808448e2316c79ec6b92398f2a7a7f81608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3, \\pm 2, \\pm 1, 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />. Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are necessary to check.\nAnother way is to observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6aed4eb1cfed0855990e1fdb4b3c160f6087c83f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3-a$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> factors into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c0c5ff681af0761d61fb663ada7a1a52b67949.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-1)a(a+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />. Any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive numbers must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6aed4eb1cfed0855990e1fdb4b3c160f6087c83f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3-a$\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> is both divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This provides an algebraic method for proving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/0/2f08da8228aea42b6adac3e93948bc700c3c151b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^3 \\equiv a \\pmod6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are not given any other requirements than the two given in the problem, so we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fbef8d105baba52528dfe2dab95dcdf1aab09a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_{2018} = a_2 + a_{2017} + \\cdots + a_{1004} + a_{1005} = \\frac{2018^{2018}}{2018} \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"454\" height=\"41\" />. Since the (theoretical) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/7/d075a0c1c59c2ddfd26914ffeec6697fb13056d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1004.5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> averages out to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ff1481eb2c29c0fa16bd2a127ac0501d0e19574.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2018^{2017}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" /> (lets call this constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />), we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fab4c15dd34904a576d61b3ab039662f34d3551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1, a_{2018}) = (N - x_1, N+x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"238\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffbc57511794e04905a8b9bd47434ae2a31fce19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_2, a_{2017}) = (N - x_2, N+x_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"238\" height=\"20\" />, ... ,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123cc6436142266c36bb081def0d35a7e690456e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{1004}, a_{1005}) = (N - x_{1004}, N+x_{1004})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"297\" height=\"20\" /> for the sequence of decreasing positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/330856ca34ce4c659fcf1d53864ebd72ceae165d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\cdots, x_{1004}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"13\" />. Notice that for any such pair (say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce73daee97a04cbe1e5d1cbe33b369f47c69acd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_{n}, a_{2019-n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />), we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eae060be4a05796daf288da03f88aa687c44a8e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_n)^3 + (a_{2019-n})^3 = (N - x_n)^3 + (N+x_n)^3 = 2N^3 + 6N\\cdot x_n \\equiv 2N^3 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"615\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/92120bac4ff8a064bffc82b552ed69c3f3b7641f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^3 + a_2^3 + \\cdots + a_{2018}^3 \\equiv 1004\\cdot 2N^3 \\equiv 2018(2018^{2017})^3 \\equiv 2018^{6052} \\equiv 2^{6052} \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"634\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/066877838d9bdddb56ddb5a1eaef0e1c8762ab61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^x \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> repeats in the pattern <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65212c82e7f5e8669732ad6a194c6db620a4eea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 4, 2, 4, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />, our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982a88b67a2e4cfdf06eb9e75b1d5ecfcd482884.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}  4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"48\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~ Lucas.xue\n</p><p>~ LaTeX corrections by Samvuong\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, note that n^3 ≡ n (mod 6) for any integer n. This is because n^3 - n = (n-1)n(n+1) is the product of three consecutive integers, ensuring divisibility by both 2 and 3.\n</p><p>Thus, Σ a_i^3 ≡ Σ a_i = 2018^2018 (mod 6).\n</p><p>Since 2018 ≡ 2 (mod 6), we have 2018^2018 ≡ 2^2018 (mod 6).\nObserving the powers of 2 modulo 6:\n2^1 ≡ 2, 2^2 ≡ 4, 2^3 ≡ 2, 2^4 ≡ 4.\nThe pattern alternates: even exponents yield 4. Since 2018 is even, 2^2018 ≡ 4 (mod 6).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba5230373c930a1e2a9c520030ccd7384a6805b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)} \\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>With Modular Arithmetic Intro\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wbv3TArroSs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wbv3TArroSs</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SRjZ6B5DR74\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SRjZ6B5DR74</a>\n</p><p>~bunny1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4_x1sgcQCp4?t=112\">https://youtu.be/4_x1sgcQCp4?t=112</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B\">2018 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017033122\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 561/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17155/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.134      1 -total\n 59.97%    7.877      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 39.12%    5.138      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15993:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017033122 and revision id 291625. Rendering